Description: Add NC12 to default preferred renderable fourccs (Pi 5 HEVC)
 Patch 0002 added the NC12 fourcc mapping but intentionally did NOT add it
 to the renderable formats list, expecting the SAND128 modifier issue to
 require multi-week GPU import work.
 .
 However, without NC12 in the renderable list, VideoDecoderPipeline::
 PickDecoderOutputFormat() rejects it as a candidate and decode init
 fails with "Failed to pick an output format" -- chromium falls back to
 software HEVC decode.
 .
 This patch adds NC12 to DefaultPreferredRenderableFourccs() so the
 candidate is accepted and decoding proceeds. Either:
   (a) the v3d driver / ANGLE EGL path on Pi 5 happens to handle the
       column-tiled NV12 buffer (best case),
   (b) we get visible corruption -- diagnostic for SAND128 modifier work,
       or
   (c) DMA-buf import fails downstream -- specific failure point to
       triage next.
 .
 Either way this advances past the current static block.
Author: chromium-rpi-hevc <build@chromium-rpi-hevc>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-04-30

--- a/media/gpu/chromeos/video_decoder_pipeline.cc
+++ b/media/gpu/chromeos/video_decoder_pipeline.cc
@@ -343,6 +343,12 @@ std::vector<Fourcc> VideoDecoderPipeline::DefaultPreferredRenderableFourccs() {
   // Preferred output formats in order of preference.
   // TODO(mcasas): query the platform for its preferred formats and modifiers.
   return {
+#if BUILDFLAG(USE_V4L2_CODEC_RPI)
+      // EXPERIMENTAL: Pi 5 BCM2712 column-tiled NV12 from rpi-hevc-dec.
+      // Listed first so it wins over plain NV12 when both are exposed.
+      // See media/gpu/chromeos/fourcc.h NC12 comment for layout caveats.
+      Fourcc(Fourcc::NC12),
+#endif
       Fourcc(Fourcc::NV12),
       Fourcc(Fourcc::P010),
       // Only used for Hana (MT8173). Remove when that device reaches EOL
